<title>SINGAPORE: Hotel Royal 1996 net profit up 3.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Hotel Royal 1996 net profit up 3.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>	  (in millons Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		 4.39    vs    4.23</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)   14.65    vs   14.11</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)	 5.0     vs    5.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		  23.32    vs   21.68</p>
<p>    Other income	     0.63    vs    0.41</p>
<p>    Interest expense	 4.22    vs    3.82</p>
<p>    Pretax		     6.95    vs    5.64</p>
<p>    Tax			  2.56    vs    1.41</p>
<p>Note - Hotel Royal Ltd said its hotel property in Singapore was revalued. The value of the land increased to Singapore S$61 million from S$39 million and the surplus of S$22 million was taken into its books in 1996.</p>
<p>The value of its hotel building increased to S$69 million from its net book value of S$3.28 million. The revaulation surplus for the building was not booked, it said.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
